WEBVTT

00:01:28.292 --> 00:01:31.254
something that never— or only—
happens in a dream.

00:01:31.671 --> 00:01:33.798
Wake up.
No, that isn’t it—

00:01:33.798 --> 00:01:35.466
you can wake up in a dream.

00:01:35.591 --> 00:01:38.761
Pinch yourself.
If it hurts, aren’t you really awake?

00:01:38.928 --> 00:01:40.596
Try to read or write something.

00:01:40.596 --> 00:01:41.889
Run around the room.

00:01:41.889 --> 00:01:45.476
Does your pace seem normal 
or suspiciously slow?

00:01:45.476 --> 00:01:47.311
Suspiciously fast?

00:01:47.311 --> 00:01:51.274
Can’t tell? Try to remember
the last time you ran.

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:54.861
Actually, that brings us 
to an even better test

00:01:54.861 --> 00:01:58.406
from the 17th century French philosopher
René Descartes.

00:01:58.614 --> 00:02:02.201
He pointed out that in our memories,
dreams are disconnected—